        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(thread-ownership): cap mention cache and bound forwarder JSON reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes two thread-ownership resource bounds in the Slack multi-agent plugin:\n\n1. **`mentionedThreads`** — in-memory mention cache with no size cap under sustained @-mention traffic.\n2. **409 ownership-conflict JSON reads** — forwarder conflict responses used unbounded `resp.json()` instead of the shared bounded provider JSON reader.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRoutes mention tracking through `pruneMapToMaxSize` (cap **1 000** entries) and replaces the 409 handler's `resp.json()` call with `readProviderJsonResponse` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/provider-http`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLong-lived gateways with high Slack @-mention volume get bounded mention-cache memory. Oversized ownership-conflict JSON bodies fail closed instead of buffering unbounded data.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/thread-ownership/index.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Mention cache grew without bound; ownership-conflict responses could allocate unbounded JSON.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS (Darwin arm64), Node.js v22.22.0, local source checkout on branch `fix/thread-ownership-cap-mentions-bound-json`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/thread-ownership/index.test.ts --reporter=verbose`\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\n ✓ evicts oldest mention cache entries once the cache exceeds its cap\n (409 conflict path uses readProviderJsonResponse in production code)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  22 passed (22)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:** After 1 001 tracked mentions the oldest `{channel}:{thread}` key is evicted; existing 409 conflict handling tests still pass with bounded JSON parsing on the production path.\n- **What was not tested:** Live Slack forwarder service or production gateway logs.\n",
        "branch": "fix/thread-ownership-cap-mentions-bound-json",
